// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/widgets/build-receipt.t27 -- one open-flow build, t27 spec to XC7A200T bitstream, as a receipt
; Source of truth for public/widgets/build-receipt/ (gHashTag/trinity): scripts/widget-pages-from-spec.mjs
; compiles this file, checks its constants, evaluates the tests below and writes the page; the page
; hands every constant to tool.js as window.T27_WIDGET. tool.js holds no English of its own: every
; word on screen is a SAY_ constant here, every number the tool relies on is a K_ constant or a field
; of receipt.json written by the same script run.
; ASCII only (L3), English only (LANG-EN).

; WHAT IT SHOWS: a shop-style receipt for one real build on one machine. Each stage of the open flow
; is a line item with its wall time, its tool and version, the size of the file it wrote and that
; file's sha256: the t27 compiler (WebAssembly, in node) turns specs/ternary/stream_ternary_mac.t27
; into Verilog, yosys synthesises it, nextpnr-xilinx places and routes it on the xc7a200tfbg676-1
; chipdb, prjxray's fasm2frames and xc7frames2bit write the bitstream, and the last line hashes it.
; Under the items: the TOTAL, a line that no vendor tool and no licence was used, the exact commands,
; and how to reproduce it. A barcode is drawn from the bitstream's sha256.

; DATA PROVENANCE: scripts/widget-data/build-receipt.mjs ran every stage in /tmp/widget-receipt and
; wrote receipt.json and the generated block below; it then re-checked that the stage times sum to
; the total within rounding and that the stage count matches the data. The datapath is generated
; from the t27 spec; the board wrapper (clock from STARTUPE2's CFGMCLK, two LFSRs as stimulus, three
; LEDs) is hand-written Verilog, scripts/widget-data/build-receipt-top.v, and the receipt says so.
; Outside the total, bitwalk (gHashTag/t27 specs/xilinx7, generated by the same compiler's rust
; target) writes a second .bit from the same frames to check xc7frames2bit's payload.

; WHAT IT DOES NOT CLAIM: that the bitstream was loaded into a board (it was not: no JTAG was run),
; that the design does anything useful on one, or that the times hold on another machine. The run
; shared the machine with other work; its load average at start is printed on the receipt. No Vivado
; was run, so there is no Vivado time to compare against.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

